A||||5||jmw||Seat Skins||||5||
Z||000000||jmw||10-24-2000||04:37 PM||||Ummm...so how do you pull / replace seat skins? I have given up on ever finding an original driver's seat in decent condition. I always thought the seats had to be reupholstered. I've never heard of this seat skin business. Could someone please enlighten me? <P>It seems like, with all the folks out there needing driver's seats, and all the orphaned passenger seats in the world, someone would figure out how to balance supply and demand. Or maybe they already have and I just don't know it.<P>Thanks!<P><BR>"Well behaved women rarely make history." - Laurel Thatcher Ulrich||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-24-2000||06:31 PM||||Contact any of the many vendors on the forum that sell parts, dismantle cars.  They have the seat skins in the color, style for the year Fiero. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif</A> <P>Don't want to add spam to the forum.||||reg||7
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-24-2000||06:54 PM||||There are a few places that sell new seat covers.  The Fiero Store sells original cloth seat covers and Mr. Mikes (...someday...) sells leather in a few different styles.  Both list for around $400.  I think the passenger side back will fit either side, but the bottoms are side specific (to a certain extent).  Since the Fiero is famous (infamous?) for wearing out at the drivers side outer bolster, you aren't going to find many drivers side backs in good shape.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-25-2000||02:05 AM||||Seat backs are interchangable. Lower seats are interchangable but you'll have 2 holes on the console side of the seats. To remove the seat skins you need a pair of pliers or side cutters. They are held on with "hogrings" You can remove the hogrings and remove the skins. It's a slow process. Reove rings peel back skin remove more rings. You will need a hogring tool and new hogrings to re-assemble. Tools and hogrings are available at most major hardware stores or upolstery shops.<BR>If you decide to buy Mr. Mikes Seats he supplies a VERY detailed video of the entire process. In fact Mr Mike supplies EVERYTHING you need to do the swap. (including the tools!!)<P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-25-2000||09:12 AM||||Check out Mr. Mike's web site for some helpful hints.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||10-25-2000||09:08 PM||||The holes on the passenger seat cover will be hidden by the console and by the seat belt guide.  We've done it and it looks good.  ||||reg||1
